invariant: INV-45
file: src/sha3.c
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: sha3_hw.c's x86-64 copy runs sha3_inverted_lanes.h's form in place
  of sha3_andn.h's, so a session that states BMI1 and BMI2 gets the round
  of a CPU without them. Every digest stays right, so no vector notices.
  test/hash-builds.sh compiles the copy for x86-64 under the pinned clang
  and requires ANDN and RORX and no NOT: the inverted lanes' chi takes
  five NOTs a round.

--- old
#define SHA3_FORM SHA3_FORM_ANDN
--- new
#define SHA3_FORM SHA3_FORM_INVERTED_LANES
